## Backends

MulleCG defines by default, which backend is going to be used (see:
[_MulleCGBackend.h](src/_MulleCGBackend.h)). This value can be overridden at
compile time. In your project, you can set this to "OpenGLES2" for example:

``` sh
mulle-sde environment set OTHER_CFLAGS "-DMULLE_CG_GLVERSION=2"
```

if you want to compile old OpenGL code, use OpenGL3_2:

``` sh
mulle-sde environment set OTHER_CFLAGS "-DMULLE_CG_GLVERSION=1"
```

| `#define`          | Value | Description                                      |
|--------------------|-------|--------------------------------------------------|
| `MULLE_CG_GL3_2`   | 1     | OpenGL 3.2, shaderless, deprecated code possible |
| `MULLE_CG_GLES2`   | 2     | OpenGLES 2, needs shader                         |
| `MULLE_CG_GLES3_2` | 3     | OpenGLES 3.2, needs shader                       |


> #### Note
>
> MulleGLFW provides OpenGL (Vulkan) etc. MulleCG brings nanovg into the picture,
> which resides on top of OpenGL. MulleCG/nanovg doesnt depend on MulleGLFW though,
> so that in the future there might be a MulleSDL and MulleCG doesn't have to
> change for it.

